               <title value="Hospital course note"/>
               <code>
                  <coding>
                     <system value="http://loinc.org"/>
                     <code value="8648-8"/>
                     <display value="Hospital course note"/>
                  </coding>
               </code>
               <text>
                  <status value="generated"/>
                  <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the hospital course of your 52-year-old female patient, who was admitted on 15/08/2021 with acute lower abdominal pain and suspected tubal pregnancy. On admission, physical examination, transvaginal ultrasonography, and serum beta-hCG measurement confirmed a right-sided tubal ectopic pregnancy without signs of rupture. Given the patient's clinical presentation and gestational findings, surgical intervention was indicated. The patient underwent laparoscopic salpingectomy with successful removal of the ectopic pregnancy. The postoperative course was uneventful. Intravenous fluid replacement and analgesic medication were administered perioperatively. Vital signs remained stable throughout the stay. The patient was discharged on 16/08/2021 in good general condition. Follow-up serum beta-hCG monitoring and outpatient gynecological review are recommended. Please do not hesitate to contact us should any questions arise.</div>
               </text>
            </section>
